{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125262-hedge-wizards-sorcerer-for-awakening","id":1125262,"title":"Hedge Wizards / Sorcerer for Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-05T10:06:26-07:00","id":1125262,"title":"Hedge Wizards / Sorcerer for Awakening","content":"Sorcerer, the Hedge Wizard's Handbook is one of my favorite oWoD books. Is there something similar for Chronicles of Darkness? I know there are merits scattered through different books, but is there a formal minor template somewhere for these guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:10:58-07:00","id":1125264,"title":"","content":"There's a few options:<br /> <br /> Proxmi are families who inherit the ability to use a fixed list of spells. Second Sight has mortal magicians (but they're really low powered). Vampire's Blood Sorcery has a vampire aligned group of mortal magic users.<br /> <br /> If you click the index in my sig there's a few groups under the new ritual system, ceremonies system, and hedge sorcery. They're not official though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:14:23-07:00","id":1125266,"title":"","content":"Thanks KIng's Raven. Unofficial is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:19:51-07:00","id":1125267,"title":"","content":"Gutter Magic from Witch Finders is also an option, one which I personally really like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:23:21-07:00","id":1125268,"title":"","content":"There is a merit for Sorcerors in Dark Eras Companion, but its, explicitly not a template. <br /> <br /> Anyone can take the Sorceror Merit, except undead (Ghosts/Vampires/Deathless/Lifeless, Prommies, Bound, and ghouls are iffy).<br /> <br /> So you can have the Sorcery merit if your human/changeling/mages/possessed/bloodbathers/pyshics/body thieves/beasts/werewolves/deviants/fetches and so on.<br /> <br /> They have open rites, which you don't need the merit for, although you can do it better with it when you choose open rite mastery, and closed rites that you need the merit for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T12:31:30-07:00","id":1125310,"title":"","content":"The Second sight book has a chapter called &quot;Low Magic&quot; that might be what your looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:39:31-07:00","id":1125355,"title":"","content":"That 1e.<br /> <br /> In 2e anyone can practice hedge magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:41:51-07:00","id":1125356,"title":"","content":"Oh I forgot Sign of Sorcery is supposed to have imbue living spell, perhaps that would grant some magic to the imbued being.<br /> <br /> Also Free Council can use mundane Hedge Wizards in their spell casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:17:23-07:00","id":1125379,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Helped, but confused, since a lot of that stuff is 1e. So where do you go to build a Hedge Mage in 2e? Or is this just something you can't officially do in CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:29:41-07:00","id":1125386,"title":"","content":"Unless the Dark Eras chapter updated it, it hasn't been officially done. There are various fan conversions, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You can also let mortals use the splat specific powers via various methods. The Pack has Magnanimous Totem that lets pack members (including humans, I think) pick up Renown and Gifts. Promethean has Alchemists (not done for PCs yet). I put something together for Hedge Sorcerers (Contracts) and mortal users of Utterances. Anyone can use Gadgets (from Demon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-05-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T16:24:44-07:00","id":1125406,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras Companion has a 2e Sorcery Merit.<br /> <br /> You get so many slots for rituals. In each slot ypu can either put in a Open Rite Mastery (no one needs the merit to do Open Rites, but taking an open rite mastery in one makes you better at it) and closed rites that you need the merit for and three things (those three things vary by rite).<br /> <br /> Example you could spend 1 rite slot on Open Rite Mastery: Exocisms and a second slot for a special closed rite spell.<br /> <br /> If having a template is important to you make a Blood Bather (there are two types given) with with Sorcery Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T16:35:09-07:00","id":1125410,"title":"","content":"Also in the core is the MCI merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T17:11:13-07:00","id":1125419,"title":"","content":"Character: Floria Species: Bloodbather<br /> <br /> Merits: Ritual Sorceror \u2022\u2022\u2022, Sorcerous Knowledge \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Rituals slots: Summoning, Warding, Exorcising, Contacting, Binding, Opening Hedgegates, Creating Akthata, (I'll finish later).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T18:01:14-07:00","id":1125427,"title":"","content":"Cool I got dark eras stuff! I'll use that.<br /> <br /> Is there a master list of 2e rituals somewhere? I would assume they're scattered everywhere.<br /> <br /> I still think someone should fan-make a Hedge Magician minor-template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"